# =============================================================================
# MASES Phase 2 UI — Portal build environment
# =============================================================================
#
# File:    mase_app/.env.portal
# Phase:   1 (Frontend foundation) — Unit 1.4
# Version: 1.0.0
# Loaded:  When `vite build --mode portal` is run (npm run
#          build:portal or npm run build:all).
# Deploys: Built output (dist-portal/) is served from
#          portal.maalearna.com.et.
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What this file is
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vite's environment file for the portal build. It is the portal
# counterpart to .env.workspace. Every decision documented in that
# file — the Vite loading order, the "public config only" rule, the
# TypeScript declaration coupling, the reserved-name namespace —
# applies here unchanged and is not repeated.
#
# If the two files ever diverge in a way this header does not
# explain, .env.workspace is the reference.
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The single difference from .env.workspace
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The portal serves a different brand voice than the workspace. The
# only VITE_-prefixed variable whose value differs between the two
# builds is VITE_APP_NAME. Everything else — the API origin, any
# future feature flags that apply to both — is identical.
#
# That identity is deliberate. Both surfaces talk to the same API,
# use the same design tokens, and share the same client bundle
# conventions. If the two files begin accumulating other
# differences, that is a signal that the two builds are diverging
# beyond a cosmetic rebrand, and the architecture deserves a
# review — the freeze treats workspace and portal as two
# presentations of the same product, not as two products.
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What MUST NOT be placed in this file
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Same rule as .env.workspace: no secrets. Every VITE_-prefixed value
# is inlined into the portal's client bundle and is visible to any
# visitor. The portal is a PUBLIC surface — the same rule applies
# with more force here than on the workspace, because the audience
# includes shareholders and any third party who reaches the login
# page.
# =============================================================================


# =============================================================================
# API base URL
# =============================================================================
#
# Identical to the workspace value. Both builds call the same API.
#
# Why the value is duplicated rather than read from a shared .env:
#
#   · A shared .env at the project root would work — Vite loads .env
#     before .env.<mode>, and .env.<mode> overrides. The base .env
#     could hold VITE_API_BASE_URL and VITE_APP_NAME's fallback, with
#     each mode file overriding only VITE_APP_NAME.
#
#   · But the duplication is intentional for reviewability. A
#     reviewer who opens this file sees exactly which API the portal
#     talks to, without needing to cross-reference another file. In
#     a production security review, "which API does this surface
#     talk to" is a question that should be answerable from a single
#     file. The cost of the duplication — two places to update if
#     the API origin ever moves — is low, and the move is not
#     anticipated.
#
#   · If the API origin ever needs to differ between workspace and
#     portal (for example, a canary deployment), the current
#     structure already supports it without refactoring.
#
# Rules for the value itself — no trailing slash, scheme required,
# no path segment — are documented in .env.workspace.
#
VITE_API_BASE_URL="https://api.maalearna.com.et"


# =============================================================================
# Application name
# =============================================================================
#
# The portal's product name, as displayed in the browser tab caption
# (fallback) and as the logo's alt text (when no explicit logoAlt prop
# is supplied).
#
# "Maale Arna Portal" is the formal, shareholder-facing name. It
# matches the <title> in portal-entry/index.html §"Why <title>Maale
# Arna Portal</title>". The workspace uses the shorter internal name
# ("MASES") because the workspace's audience is staff, not
# shareholders.
#
# The choice of brand voice per surface is documented in
# portal-entry/index.html. This variable is the runtime reflection
# of that choice.
#
VITE_APP_NAME="ማሴስ ባለአክሲዮኖች ፓርታል"


# =============================================================================
# Reserved for future use (do not uncomment without a code change)
# =============================================================================
#
# The reserved namespace and the rules for using it are documented in
# .env.workspace. If a future change adds a VITE_-prefixed variable
# that applies to both builds, add it to both files with the same
# value and to .env.workspace first — the workspace's documentation
# is the reference. If it applies to the portal only, document it
# here.
#
# =============================================================================